WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.554 --> 00:00:13.835
rescuer was Miles.

2
00:00:13.855 --> 00:00:17.378
"This is a matter for the law to take care of."

3
00:00:18.999 --> 00:00:22.302
Miles held onto the blacksmith's arm until he released Edward.

4
00:00:22.322 --> 00:00:24.123
"Not you."

5
00:00:25.945 --> 00:00:29.448
The blacksmith rubbed his arm as Edward leaped to Miles' side.

6
00:00:30.664 --> 00:00:33.306
"I appreciate your rescuing me," Edward said.

7
00:00:33.326 --> 00:00:36.708
"But you took your time getting here, Sir Miles."

8
00:00:36.728 --> 00:00:39.949
"Sir Miles!

9
00:00:40.430 --> 00:00:42.011
I forgot that Edward made me a knight."

10
00:00:43.311 --> 00:00:44.652
Miles smiled to himself.

11
00:00:44.672 --> 00:00:47.774
"He's such a brave, spirited boy.

12
00:00:49.975 --> 00:00:54.277
I'm honored to be a knight—even if his kingdom is only an imaginary one."

13
00:00:55.658 --> 00:00:58.600
Miles' thoughts were interrupted by the arrival of the sheriff.

14
00:01:00.012 --> 00:01:01.873
"This must be the boy who stole the ham."

15
00:01:03.233 --> 00:01:04.893
The sheriff took out his handcuffs.

16
00:01:04.913 --> 00:01:07.194
"Don't handcuff him!"

17
00:01:07.554 --> 00:01:08.254
Miles said.

18
00:01:08.274 --> 00:01:11.015
"He'll go quietly to see the judge."

19
00:01:12.696 --> 00:01:15.696
But Edward was outraged and refused to move.

20
00:01:16.657 --> 00:01:18.497
"The king does not go to court!"

21
00:01:18.517 --> 00:01:25.039
"You can't expect your subjects to obey the law, if you won't," Miles said.

22
00:01:25.059 --> 00:01:28.600
"Hmm," Edward said.

23
00:01:29.632 --> 00:01:30.533
"You may be right.

24
00:01:31.633 --> 00:01:35.316
This will give me a chance to see how criminals are treated."

25
00:01:38.618 --> 00:01:41.941
Inside the courtroom the woman told her story to the judge.

26
00:01:43.261 --> 00:01:45.223
He quickly convicted Edward of theft.

27
00:01:46.644 --> 00:01:49.125
Miles gasped, but Edward stayed calm.

28
00:01:49.146 --> 00:01:54.409
"The poor boy doesn't realize he'll go to jail," Miles thought.

29
00:01:54.429 --> 00:01:58.312
"How much is this ham worth?"

30
00:01:58.856 --> 00:02:00.077
the judge asked the woman.

31
00:02:00.097 --> 00:02:03.559
"Five dollars," she said.

32
00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:05.880
The judge frowned.

33
00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:08.322
"Perhaps you'd like to think again.

34
00:02:08.342 --> 00:02:13.765
He's an ignorant lad, who was probably driven to steal by hunger."

35
00:02:14.785 --> 00:02:16.947
The woman folded her arms across her chest.

36
00:02:16.967 --> 00:02:22.370
"No, that's what the ham is worth, and he needs to be taught a lesson."

37
00:02:24.431 --> 00:02:26.052
The judge shifted in his seat.

38
00:02:27.104 --> 00:02:32.848
"You do know that the punishment for stealing anything over three dollars is life in prison?"

39
00:02:34.609 --> 00:02:39.793
Wide-eyed with fear, Edward looked at Miles, but Miles was too startled to comfort him.

40
00:02:39.813 --> 00:02:42.614
"Oh, what have I done?"

41
00:02:43.035 --> 00:02:43.855
the woman cried.

42
00:02:43.875 --> 00:02:47.698
"I don't want the boy to spend his life in prison!"

43
00:02:47.718 --> 00:02:53.822
"I haven't officially recorded the ham's value," the judge said.

44
00:02:53.842 --> 00:02:56.764
"There's still time for you to change it."

45
00:02:58.604 --> 00:02:59.145
"Oh, yes!

46
00:02:59.605 --> 00:03:03.268
Now that I think again, it's worth only a dollar at most."

47
00:03:03.288 --> 00:03:05.929
"That's better."

48
00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:07.911
The judge smiled.

49
00:03:09.752 --> 00:03:12.834
Miles hugged Edward, who let the big man embrace him.

50
00:03:14.636 --> 00:03:19.139
But when the judge sentenced him to five days in jail, Edward started to protest.

51
00:03:19.159 --> 00:03:23.342
"Hush!" Miles whispered as the judge stood up to leave.

52
00:03:23.362 --> 00:03:26.344
"Don't make the judge change his mind."

53
00:03:27.588 --> 00:03:31.169
"I didn't steal anything, so I shouldn't have to go to prison."

54
00:03:32.369 --> 00:03:33.470
Edward stamped his foot.

55
00:03:35.790 --> 00:03:39.371
Miles nodded but was busy watching the sheriff approach the woman.

56
00:03:39.391 --> 00:03:43.453
"I wonder what that fellow is up to."

57
00:03:44.953 --> 00:03:47.734
Miles walked over to where the sheriff and the woman were talking.

58
00:03:47.754 --> 00:03:51.515
"That's a fine ham," the sheriff said.

59
00:03:51.535 --> 00:03:54.696
"I'll buy it from you for a dollar."

60
00:03:56.288 --> 00:03:58.229
The woman was insulted by his offer.

61
00:03:58.249 --> 00:04:03.693
"I only said it was worth a dollar to spare the boy from life in prison.

62
00:04:04.793 --> 00:04:06.414
I paid five dollars for it."

63
00:04:06.434 --> 00:04:10.957
"So, you lied when you said it was worth a dollar!"

64
00:04:11.237 --> 00:04:12.678
the sheriff said triumphantly.

65
00:04:12.698 --> 00:04:17.121
"I guess the boy will spend the rest of his life in prison after all."

66
00:04:17.141 --> 00:04:19.342
"No, no!"

67
00:04:20.523 --> 00:04:22.304
The woman shook her head in confusion.

68
00:04:23.484 --> 00:04:27.685
Miles realized that the sheriff was trying to trick her, but he didn't say anything.

69
00:04:29.226 --> 00:04:33.407
After watching the woman sell the ham for a dollar, he returned to Edward's side.

70
00:04:33.427 --> 00:04:38.669
"I refuse to go to jail even for only five days."

71
00:04:39.729 --> 00:04:41.309
Edward stubbornly crossed his arms.

72
00:04:41.329 --> 00:04:45.711
"Don't worry, I have a plan," Miles said.

73
00:04:45.731 --> 00:04:50.352
"Just trust me, and we'll soon be on our way to my family's home."

74
00:04:52.408 --> 00:04:56.410
Having quickly hidden the ham, the sheriff was ready to escort Edward to jail.

75
00:04:56.430 --> 00:04:59.512
"Sheriff, we need to talk."

76
00:05:00.873 --> 00:05:02.974
Miles put his arm around the man's shoulders.

77
00:05:02.994 --> 00:05:07.937
"Perhaps you could look the other way while this boy escapes."

78
00:05:07.957 --> 00:05:11.099
"But I'd be committing a crime!"

79
00:05:11.459 --> 00:05:12.259
the sheriff said.

80
00:05:12.279 --> 00:05:15.781
"I should arrest you for even suggesting that!"

81
00:05:17.342 --> 00:05:19.423
"Or perhaps you'll be arrested."

82
00:05:19.883 --> 00:05:20.724
Miles paused.

83
00:05:22.072 --> 00:05:25.075
"I heard you trick the woman into selling you her ham.

84
00:05:26.736 --> 00:05:29.018
Do you want me to tell the judge about that?"

85
00:05:29.038 --> 00:05:32.081
"Oh, I was just joking with her!"

86
00:05:34.983 --> 00:05:36.504
The sheriff laughed nervously.

87
00:05:36.524 --> 00:05:40.047
"Really?" Miles said loudly.

88
00:05:40.067 --> 00:05:44.891
"You do know the penalty for breaking that law is death?"

89
00:05:47.353 --> 00:05:48.034
"What law?"

90
00:05:48.895 --> 00:05:50.196
The sheriff looked frightened.

91
00:05:51.776 --> 00:05:55.658
"The one against paying too little for big pieces of meat.

92
00:05:57.119 --> 00:06:00.741
You'd better return that ham to the woman and let Edward go."

93
00:06:00.761 --> 00:06:02.822
"Of course!

94
00:06:02.942 --> 00:06:03.443
Right away!"

95
00:06:04.103 --> 00:06:05.184
The sheriff hurried off.

96
00:06:05.204 --> 00:06:09.866
"I'll tell the judge that the boy simply disappeared."

97
00:06:09.886 --> 00:06:11.247
"Thank you!"

98
00:06:11.807 --> 00:06:12.528
Miles said.

99
00:06:12.548 --> 00:06:17.070
"How did you know about that law?"

100
00:06:17.511 --> 00:06:19.332
Edward asked as they left the courtroom.

101
00:06:20.774 --> 00:06:21.679
Miles smiled.

102
00:06:21.699 --> 00:06:23.066
"I made it up!"
